.TH SYSTEMD\-RECALL\-QUERY\-SERVICE.SERVICE 8 "2026-03-23" "systemd-recalld 0.1.0" "System Manager"
.SH NAME
systemd-recall-query-service.service, systemd-recall-query-service \- AI-powered query service for captured data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-recall-query-service
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-recall-query-service
provides a REST API for querying data captured by
.BR systemd-recalld (8).
It uses AI models (Whisper for audio, CLIP for video, BERT for text,
Flamingo for multimodal) to process and search through captured content.
.PP
Authentication is handled via PAM with JWT tokens for API access.
The API supports TLS encryption and rate limiting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " PATH" "\fR, \fP" \-\-config= PATH
Path to configuration file. Defaults to
.IR /etc/systemd/recall-query-service/recall-query-service.conf .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/auth
Authenticate with username and password. Returns a JWT token.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/query
Submit a natural language query. Requires Bearer token authentication.
.SH CONFIGURATION
See
.I /etc/systemd/recall-query-service/recall-query-service.conf
for configuration options including API settings, AI model paths,
authentication, and storage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/recall-query-service/recall-query-service.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/recall-query-service/jwt-secret
JWT signing secret (must be generated before first use).
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/systemd-recall
PAM configuration for authentication.
.TP
.I /var/lib/systemd/recall-query-service/
Default storage and model directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recallctl (1),
.BR systemd-recalld (8),
.BR systemd (1)
.SH LICENSE
LGPL-2.1-or-later
